rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates separation of concerns where CAS Runner orchestrates, Workflows
    reason, and Knowledge Providers handle access. Workflows must not perform repository
    scanning or direct file writes.
  title: Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Distinguishes between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution) and decision
    status (governance lifecycle), ensuring consistent interpretation across the Architecture
    Evolution Map.
  title: Pattern and Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All new patterns must be initialized with a 'supporting' scope to ensure
    they are validated through usage and evidence before being considered for 'core'
    promotion.
  title: Patterns Must Be Created as Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the merging or consolidation of patterns across different architectural
    layers to maintain separation between governance, execution, contracts, and reliability.
  title: Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core status must be backed by strong evidence from
    multiple sources to ensure the core architecture remains stable and reliable.
  title: Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes Architecture Work as the authoritative source of planning state;
    generated artifacts must derive status from this registry rather than maintaining
    independent state.
  title: Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all architectural decisions to be documented using a specific
    structured YAML schema to enable machine processing and system-wide consistency.
  title: Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared knowledge workspace and are prohibited
    from duplicating workspace-level governance structures when existing ones are
    available.
  title: Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines mandatory semantic distinctions for architecture artifacts, separating
    intent from state and architect decisions from final governance approval.
  title: Language & Semantics Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures traceability by requiring all patterns derived from heuristics
    to be linked to at least one observed signal as grounding evidence.
  title: Heuristic-Derived Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines the absolute hierarchy for rule resolution: Global Rules > Project
    Rules > Prompt Rules. Higher precedence rules cannot be overridden by lower levels.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control by requiring that all system-generated
    architectural proposals be explicitly accepted, rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: System Proposes, Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts like AEM or AID must summarize authoritative
    sources and cannot serve as the durable primary source of state.
  title: Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that architecture decisions be recorded exclusively in Architecture
    Decision Records (ADR); all other representations must be derived from these records.
  title: ADR as Single Source of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines mandatory criteria for signal-to-pattern promotion: recurrence,
    system impact, reusability, and stability must all be satisfied and evidenced.'
  title: Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures traceability by requiring all architectural decisions to be persisted
    as structured ADR files before they are reflected in the AEM or other system artifacts.
  title: Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any architecture item (e.g., DONE, NEXT, FUTURE)
    must be mapped directly from its governance decision status to ensure consistency.
  title: Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires the Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) to reflect and never contradict
    the official status recorded in Architecture Decision Records (ADR).
  title: AEM Consistency with Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Restricts 'core' pattern classification to foundational architectural primitives,
    preventing context-specific strategies or implementations from becoming foundational.
  title: Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
